ABSTRACT

A5 specifies the VERIFY gate. A1 specifies the FSM that transitions through it. A3 specifies plans that reference actions. A4 specifies the state that actions modify.

None of these specify what an action is.

This document specifies the action schema and the action library. An action is the atomic unit of agency: a deterministic, bounded, verifiable transition from one state to another, with declared preconditions, declared effects, declared envelope, and declared cost.

Actions do not compose. Plans compose actions (A3 §5). Actions are atomic. This is the design decision that keeps the schema finite, the library enumerable, and the verification tractable.

Status: Specification. No reference implementation. No hardware validation. Machine verification pending.

