10. FORMAL PROPERTIES

The properties A2 contributes to the Verifiable Agency Theorem:

Property A2.1 (Finiteness). The action library A is finite. (Obligation O1.)

Proof. By Rule §7.3, |A| ≤ N_A. □

Property A2.2 (Schema Totality). Every action in A has a complete schema.

Proof. By §8.2, schema completeness is a burn-time check. Actions lacking completeness are rejected. □

Property A2.3 (Effect Determinism). Every action's effect is a deterministic function.

Proof. By Rule A2-D. □

Property A2.4 (Effect Boundedness). Every action's effect evaluates in bounded time.

Proof. By Proposition A2-E. □

Property A2.5 (Committability Decidability). For every (s, a), committability is decidable in bounded time.

Proof. By Property A2-C. □

These are the A2 obligations to the Verifiable Agency Theorem. Combined with A1, A3, A4, A5, the theorem's premises are fully grounded.

