12. OPEN DESIGN TENSIONS

Honest labeling. These are unresolved in A2 v1.0.

# Question Impact
1 Action parameter representation. Actions may have parameters (e.g., delta for a brake command). How are parameters represented in the schema? As fields in the action? As part of the effect? Affects effect expressiveness.
2 Cross-type actions. Some actions are both ACTUATE and COMMUNICATE (e.g., a brake command that also logs to a remote system). Can types compose? If not, deployments must split into two actions — which may break atomicity.
3 Effect parameterization. effect(a) currently takes a state and returns a state. If actions have parameters, effect must take (s, params). Interacts with (1).
4 The REQUEST_HUMAN blocking semantics. Does the FSM block until human input, or does it log the request and continue? Affects T-AET and termination.
5 Version coexistence. Multiple versions of the same action ID can coexist. Which one does a plan reference? Needs a version-selection rule (similar to A3 §3.4).
6 Envelope abort at runtime. The abort condition is evaluated during execution. How does this interact with the FSM's atomic COMMIT state? May require a new FSM state (ABORT_CHECK).
7 Signature scheme. SK-1024 is referenced but not specified in this document. Needs cross-reference to the SK-1024 spec.
8 Burn-time verifier formalization. The verifier is named but not specified. Future spec (suggested: A2.1 — Burn-Time Verification).

None are fatal. All must be resolved before A2 v2.0.

